From: Security Fix <security@apache.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix JavaScript configuration bypass vulnerability (CVE-XXXX-XXXXX)

Prevent attackers from bypassing JavaScript security settings by injecting
JavaScriptConfig through empty JSON keys. This vulnerability allowed
authenticated users to execute arbitrary code by providing a malicious
payload with an empty key ("") containing {"enabled": true}.

The fix adds:
1. @JsonIgnoreProperties to ignore empty string keys
2. Validation to ensure JavaScriptConfig is never null
3. Security checks in all JavaScript-enabled classes

